<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Leer has higher first-half net.</title>
<headline>Van Leer has higher first-half net.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     1.49 vs  1.08</p>
<p>    Int div (guilders)		   0.25 vs  n/a</p>
<p>    Pref div				 2.00 vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net profit			    47    vs  38</p>
<p>    Net for common shrs		 45    vs  38</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  2.06 vs   2.03</p>
<p>NOTE - Royal Packaging Industries Van Leer, which was floated on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange, previously said it expected further profit growth in 1996.  </p>
<p>Operating profit before interest</p>
<p>    and tax				 105.0 vs 95.0</p>
<p>    Net operating profit		 53.0 vs 44.0</p>
<p>    Tax					17.0 vs 16.0</p>
<p>    Third party interest charge	 6.0 vs 6.0 charge</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
